{"status":"ok","message-type":"work","message-version":"1.0.0","message":{"indexed":{"date-parts":[[2026,3,14]],"date-time":"2026-03-14T06:28:55Z","timestamp":1773469735923,"version":"3.50.1"},"reference-count":48,"publisher":"Wiley","issue":"1","license":[{"start":{"date-parts":[[2000,1,18]],"date-time":"2000-01-18T00:00:00Z","timestamp":948153600000},"content-version":"vor","delay-in-days":0,"URL":"http:\/\/onlinelibrary.wiley.com\/termsAndConditions#vor"}],"content-domain":{"domain":[],"crossmark-restriction":false},"short-container-title":["FEBS Letters"],"published-print":{"date-parts":[[2000,1,21]]},"abstract":"<jats:p>No ligand has hitherto been designated for the Eph receptor tyrosine kinase family member, EphB6. Here, expression of an EphB6 ligand in the pro\u2010B leukemic cell line, Reh, is demonstrated by binding of soluble EphB6\u2010Fc fusion protein to the Reh cells. The ligand belongs to the subgroup of membrane spanning ligands, as suggested by the fact that phosphatidylinositol\u2010specific phospholipase C treatment did not abrogate binding of EphB6\u2010Fc. Two transmembrane Eph receptor ligands, ephrin\u2010B1 and ephrin\u2010B2, were identified in Reh cells. Analysis of EphB6\u2010Fc fusion protein binding to ephrin\u2010B1 or ephrin\u2010B2 transfected COS cells revealed a high\u2010affinity saturable binding between EphB6\u2010Fc and ephrin\u2010B2, but not with ephrin\u2010B1. In mice, EphB6 has previously been shown to be expressed in thymus. Here, we show expression of EphB6 in human thymus, as well as the expression of ephrin\u2010B2 in both human and mouse thymus. We conclude that ephrin\u2010B2 may be a physiological ligand for the EphB6 receptor.<\/jats:p>","DOI":"10.1016\/s0014-5793(99)01793-7","type":"journal-article","created":{"date-parts":[[2002,7,25]],"date-time":"2002-07-25T17:52:27Z","timestamp":1027619547000},"page":"169-174","source":"Crossref","is-referenced-by-count":36,"title":["Ephrin\u2010B2 is a candidate ligand for the Eph receptor, EphB6"],"prefix":"10.1002","volume":"466","author":[{"given":"Else","family":"Munthe","sequence":"first","affiliation":[],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]},{"given":"Edith","family":"Rian","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]},{"given":"Toril","family":"Holien","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]},{"given":"Anne-Marie","family":"Rasmussen","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]},{"given":"Finn Olav","family":"Levy","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]},{"given":"Hans-Christian","family":"Aasheim","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]}],"member":"311","published-online":{"date-parts":[[2000,1,18]]},"reference":[{"key":"e_1_2_5_2_1","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1016\/0896-6273(92)90177-F"},{"key":"e_1_2_5_3_1","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1146\/annurev.bi.57.070188.002303"},{"key":"e_1_2_5_4_1","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1146\/annurev.neuro.21.1.309"},{"key":"e_1_2_5_5_1","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1242\/dev.126.10.2033"},{"key":"e_1_2_5_6_1","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1016\/S0959-4388(99)80008-7"},{"key":"e_1_2_5_7_1","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1016\/S0163-7258(97)00112-5"},{"key":"e_1_2_5_8_1","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1016\/S0955-0674(97)80113-5"},{"key":"e_1_2_5_9_1","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1016\/S0896-6273(00)80276-7"},{"key":"e_1_2_5_10_1","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1038\/383722a0"},{"key":"e_1_2_5_11_1","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1126\/science.275.5306.1640"},{"key":"e_1_2_5_12_1","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1016\/S0092-8674(00)81131-9"},{"key":"e_1_2_5_13_1","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1016\/0092-8674(95)9042